      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>To the best of my ability, this is a faithful transcription of the תְּחִנָה לְשַׁבָּת מְבָרְכִים רֹאשׁ חוֺדֶשׁ סִיוָן (“Tkhine for Shabbat Mevorkhim Rosh Ḥodesh Sivan”) which appeared in תחנות מקרא קודש (<tei:hi rend="italic">Teḥinot Miqra Ḳodesh</tei:hi>, Widow and Brothers Romm, Vilna 1877) before its adaptation in Shas Tkhine Ḥadashe (Ben-Tsiyon Alfes 1910), the source from which this translation was made. English translation adapted slightly from <tei:hi rend="italic">Techinas: A Voice from the Heart “As Only A Woman Can Pray”</tei:hi> by Rivka Zakutinsky (Aura Press, 1992). –A.N. Varady</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_15403_notes"/>
